<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  SageFs as a launchd user agent (macOS). Install it from the repo root. This is
  the same block as the README's, and a test keeps the two identical:

    dotnet_root="$(dirname "$(realpath "$(command -v dotnet)")")"
    if [ -x "$dotnet_root/dotnet" ]; then
      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs 2>/dev/null
      mkdir -p ~/Library/LaunchAgents ~/Library/Logs/sagefs "$HOME/Library/Application Support/sagefs-daemon"
      sed -e "s|@HOME@|$HOME|g" -e "s|@DOTNET_ROOT@|$dotnet_root|g" \
        contrib/launchd/io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs.plist \
        > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs.plist
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs.plist
    else
      echo "No dotnet found through PATH, so nothing was installed. realpath needs macOS 12.3 or later." >&2
    fi

  The daemon then outlives every agent, terminal and editor, and comes back at
  login.

  launchd expands no variables in a plist: not ~, not $HOME. So the file in the
  repo holds two placeholders, and the sed line above fills them in. @HOME@ is
  your home directory. @DOTNET_ROOT@ is the folder that holds the real dotnet
  executable, found through PATH with symlinks resolved. The tool's launcher
  finds the runtime through DOTNET_ROOT, and launchd does not read your shell
  profile, so it is set here. The install checks that folder really holds
  dotnet before it writes anything: without dotnet on PATH, or on a macOS older
  than 12.3 (which has no realpath), it would otherwise write a plist that
  looks fine and cannot start.

  If you move or upgrade .NET to a different folder, run the install again. It
  unloads the old agent first, because launchd keeps a loaded agent's settings
  until it is unloaded, and a second bootstrap fails while the first is loaded.
  It unloads before it rewrites the plist: rewriting a loaded agent's plist and
  then unloading it made the next bootstrap fail about one time in four.

  ProgramArguments assumes SageFs is installed as a global tool, which puts the
  executable at ~/.dotnet/tools/sagefs.

  The daemon's working directory is NOT your home directory. A request that
  names no working directory (a session create, get_available_projects) falls
  back to the daemon's own cwd, so a daemon started in $HOME hands $HOME out as
  a session root. SageFs refuses to watch a home directory, so a session rooted
  there gets no hot reload and no live testing. launchd does not create a
  working directory, which is why the mkdir line above does. It is a sibling of
  ~/Library/Application Support/SageFs, where the daemon writes its own log,
  and not inside it, so the daemon never watches its own writes. Open your
  sessions in a project directory.

  Two layers restart it. The supervised flag runs a watchdog that starts a new
  daemon whenever the daemon process is gone, whatever its exit code, so
  `sagefs stop` gets you a fresh daemon. KeepAlive with SuccessfulExit false
  restarts the watchdog itself if it crashes, the same as Restart=on-failure in
  the systemd unit. A watchdog that gives up after repeated crashes exits 0, and
  launchd leaves it down.

  To stop it:   launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs
  To restart:   launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>io.github.willehrendreich.sagefs</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>@HOME@/.dotnet/tools/sagefs</string>
    <string>--supervised</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>DOTNET_ROOT</key>
    <string>@DOTNET_ROOT@</string>
  </dict>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>@HOME@/Library/Application Support/sagefs-daemon</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>5</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>@HOME@/Library/Logs/sagefs/sagefs.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>@HOME@/Library/Logs/sagefs/sagefs.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
